From: Marcin Krystianc <marcin.krystianc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NFSD: Accept an empty access ACL in NFS_ACL SETACL

The xdrgen SETACL decoders reject a request that sets NA_ACL with an
access ACL of zero entries, and nfsd3_proc_setacl() answers
ACL3ERR_INVAL. The Linux NFSv3 client sends exactly that request when
it creates a directory under a default ACL whose inherited access ACL
is equivalent to the new mode: posix_acl_create() returns a NULL
access ACL with a non-NULL default ACL, and __nfs3_proc_setacls()
sends mask NFS_ACL|NFS_DFACL with aclcnt 0. mkdir(2) then fails with
EINVAL although the server has created the directory. xfstests
generic/319 and generic/697 fail over NFSv3.

The decoders these replace, nfs3svc_decode_setaclargs() and
nfsaclsvc_decode_setaclargs(), used nfs_stream_decode_acl(), which
decodes zero entries as a NULL ACL. The SETACL procedures passed it to
set_posix_acl(), which removes the access ACL. Do the same: drop the
zero-count check, so an empty access list publishes NULL as an empty
default list already does.

Fixes: ae1f4d75a973 ("NFSD: Implement NFS-ACL v3 ACL encoding and decoding with xdrgen")
Fixes: 2125d74330f5 ("NFSD: Implement NFS-ACL v2 ACL encoding and decoding with xdrgen")
Signed-off-by: Marcin Krystianc <marcin.krystianc@gmail.com>
---
The v3 check is reached from 96ce1cc333bc ("NFSD: Use xdrgen XDR
functions for the NFS-ACL v3 SETACL procedure"), when SETACL starts
using the new decoder.

Tested on nfsd-testing 8489270d1cb9, knfsd and the NFS client in one
UML kernel over loopback, NFSv3 sec=sys, xfstests -g acl: 13 of 15
pass without this patch (generic/319, generic/697 fail), 15 of 15 with
it. Applies unchanged to nfsd-testing 194069b5ff38. The NFS_ACLv2
change is not exercised: the Linux client sends no NFS_ACLv2 SETACL.

diff --git a/fs/nfsd/nfs2acl.c b/fs/nfsd/nfs2acl.c
index 8b6e3d717217..ed41fc6dbcff 100644
--- a/fs/nfsd/nfs2acl.c
+++ b/fs/nfsd/nfs2acl.c
@@ -612,11 +612,11 @@ bool nfs_acl2_secattr_decode_begin(struct xdrgen_aggregate_cursor *c)
 			argp->invalid = true;
 			return true;
 		}
-		if (!dfacl && !c->count) {
-			argp->invalid = true;
-			return true;
-		}
-		/* An empty default list publishes NULL: default ACL removal. */
+		/*
+		 * An empty list publishes NULL, which set_posix_acl() takes
+		 * as removal: of the default ACL, or of the access ACL,
+		 * leaving only the mode bits.
+		 */
 		if (c->count) {
 			*pacl = posix_acl_alloc(c->count, GFP_KERNEL);
 			if (!*pacl)
